// The solution to the second exercise of the platforms chapter: a disabled
// branch may call a function that exists nowhere.
//
// The `cfg(macos)` block is removed on Windows and Linux before the compiler
// resolves a single name, so `a_function_that_exists_nowhere` is never
// looked up. The program compiles on both, which is the whole point of
// `cfg`.

fn main() {
    cfg(macos) {
        a_function_that_exists_nowhere();
    }
    print("compiled");
}
